# Branching

`v-rust` is the target branch for this repository, even though it is not the GitHub default branch. Treat it the way you would treat `main`.

Never commit to `v-rust` directly. Never push commits to `v-rust`. Changes reach it only through merged pull requests.

## Where a new branch starts

- By default, create the new branch from the latest branch: the branch currently checked out, which is the top of the current stack. Do not use this when the current branch is `v-rust`.
- When the user asks for a fresh branch, or the current branch is `v-rust`, create it from the latest `origin/v-rust`. Run `git fetch origin v-rust` first.

## Stacked pull requests

Prefer stacked pull requests. Each branch's pull request targets the branch it was created from. Only the bottom branch of a stack targets `v-rust`.

A fresh branch from `v-rust` starts a separate stack. Later branches created from it stack on that line, not on the earlier stack.
